As no candidate won a majority, a runoff was held between the top two finishers, Molly Mitchell Spearman and Sally Atwater. Atwater was considered to be the frontrunner,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://politicalwire.com/archives/2014/06/16/interview_of_the_day.html |title=Interview of the Day |publisher=Political Wire |date=June 16, 2014 |access-date=July 25, 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140618210810/http://politicalwire.com/archives/2014/06/16/interview_of_the_day.html |archive-date=June 18, 2014 }}</ref> until she called conservative talk show host Russ Cassell on [[WYRD-FM|News Radio WORD]] to talk about her candidacy. In the "awkward", "evasive" and "awful, incomprehensible, it-should-force-her-to-drop-out-of-the-race" interview, she seemed unable to give answers to basic questions about sex education and the teaching of evolution, to Cassell's amazement. After Atwater hung up, Cassell concluded: "Folks, I don't want to be brutal, I don't want to be mean. What you have just heard is an example of a person running for public office on name recognition only, who is clueless." Atwater subsequently apologized for her performance and the interview, which was uploaded to [[YouTube]], went viral.<ref>{{YouTube|Bi4vBdZyQe0|Sally Atwater's terrifying interview on WORD Radio}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/blogs/the-fix/wp/2014/06/16/want-to-hear-a-really-awkward-interview-with-a-politician/ |title=Want to hear a really awkward interview with a politician? |newspaper=The Washington Post |date=June 16, 2014 |access-date=July 25, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.patheos.com/blogs/friendlyatheist/2014/06/16/sally-atwater-r-running-for-superintendent-of-education-in-sc-cant-answer-basic-education-related-questions/ |title=Sally Atwater (R), Running for Superintendent of Education in SC, Can't Answer Basic Education-Related Questions |publisher=Patheos |date=June 16, 2014 |access-date=July 25, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.postandcourier.com/article/20140617/PC1603/140619398 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140721024402/http://www.postandcourier.com/article/20140617/PC1603/140619398 |url-status=dead |archive-date=July 21, 2014 |title=Sally Atwater responds to stories about radio interview (has audio) |publisher=The Post and Courier |date=June 17, 2014 |access-date=July 25, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.charlestoncitypaper.com/TheBattery/archives/2014/06/19/sally-atwater-clarifies-her-stances-on-sex-ed-evolution |title=Sally Atwater clarifies her stances on sex ed, evolution |publisher=Charleston City Paper |date=June 19, 2014 |access-date=July 25, 2014}}</ref> Atwater subsequently declined to debate Spearman before the runoff, with a spokesman for Spearman saying that "given [Atwater's] debate performance in the primary and her recent radio interview on WORD-FM, we can understand why she has made this political calculation.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.thestate.com/2014/06/16/3512017/sally-atwater-declines-etv-debate.html |title=Sally Atwater declines ETV debate before superintendent of education runoff |publisher=The State |date=June 16, 2014 |access-date=July 25, 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140724102057/http://www.thestate.com/2014/06/16/3512017/sally-atwater-declines-etv-debate.html |archive-date=July 24, 2014 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Atwater was also the subject of a lawsuit alleging that as a teacher she "routinely harassed, physically assaulted, and psychologically tormented" a disabled student.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mediaite.com/online/sally-atwater-accused-of-shoving-a-special-needs-child/ |title=Lawsuit Alleges Sally Atwater Shoved a Special Needs Child |publisher=Mediaite |date=June 21, 2014 |access-date=July 30, 2014}}</ref> Atwater's campaign dismissed the lawsuit as "baseless and frivolous".<ref>{{Cite news|url=http://www.huffingtonpost.com/2014/06/23/sally-atwater-lawsuit_n_5522253.html |title=Republican Sally Atwater Faces Lawsuit Alleging She Shoved Student Who Wanted Candy |date=June 23, 2014 |access-date=July 30, 2014|newspaper=Huffington Post |last1=McCabe |first1=David }}</ref>

